{
  "_doc": [
    "THE PLANE-HOOK ISOMORPHISM ALLOWLIST — the accepted per-hook asymmetries across the installed",
    "planes, read by crates/busbar/tests/plane_isomorphism.rs (Assertion I2 of",
    "docs/design/playbook/gate-isomorphism.md).",
    "",
    "The test REFLECTS the actual Some/None of each installed &'static PlaneDecl (it does not re-read",
    "this file to decide the matrix). For every hook field where one plane is Some and a sibling is",
    "None, the None is FORBIDDEN unless it is declared here AND the named capability maps to a real",
    "cell in qa/capability-equality.json for that plane's ledger column(s). An undeclared asymmetric",
    "None is RED (a plane silently not doing what a sibling does). A declared row that is NOT actually",
    "an asymmetric None on the live decls is also RED (a stale exemption). Over- and under-count both",
    "fail, so the file cannot drift from the decls.",
    "",
    "Each row: { field, planes_none[], capability, reason }. `field` is a PlaneDecl Option hook;",
    "`planes_none` are the installed plane keys whose None is legitimate; `capability` is the",
    "qa/capability-equality.json capability whose cell contextualizes the absence; `reason` is the",
    "one-line argument a reviewer can disagree with. Voice is NOT installed in the binary/this test",
    "target (off-default, feature-gated), so its skeleton asymmetries are governed by the no-deferral",
    "gate + the ledger's voice pin, not by this reflection — see the test header."
  ],
  "asymmetries": [
    { "field": "routes",            "planes_none": ["llm"],        "capability": "catalogue",     "reason": "the LLM plane is the fallback data-plane: it answers on the neutral completion ingress, not plane-mounted routes, so it declares no route hook" },
    { "field": "admin_routes",      "planes_none": ["llm"],        "capability": "catalogue",     "reason": "the LLM `pools:` section is not a 1.5.3 named-definition-map, so the plane has no per-registration admin surface to mount" },
    { "field": "openapi",           "planes_none": ["llm"],        "capability": "catalogue",     "reason": "the LLM plane contributes no plane-owned OpenAPI path document; its surface is the core completion API, not a plane fragment" },
    { "field": "hydrate",           "planes_none": ["llm"],        "capability": "disposition",   "reason": "the LLM plane holds no durable per-registration state to restore on boot; there is nothing to hydrate" },
    { "field": "start",             "planes_none": ["llm", "mcp"], "capability": "disposition",   "reason": "neither the LLM nor MCP plane runs a long-lived start-time task; only the A2A server plane starts a background loop" },
    { "field": "config_validate",   "planes_none": ["llm"],        "capability": "catalogue",     "reason": "the LLM `pools:` grammar is validated by core's pool config path, not by a plane-owned config_validate hook" },
    { "field": "registry_contains", "planes_none": ["llm"],        "capability": "catalogue",     "reason": "the LLM plane keeps no named-registration registry to answer containment on; its pools are core-owned config" },
    { "field": "reresolve_gates",   "planes_none": ["llm"],        "capability": "trust-pinning", "reason": "the LLM plane pins no per-peer artifact, so there are no container gates to re-resolve on a swap" },
    { "field": "retain_verify_gates","planes_none": ["llm"],       "capability": "trust-pinning", "reason": "the LLM plane retains no verify gates because it holds no pinned peer artifacts across generations" },
    { "field": "default_section",   "planes_none": ["llm"],        "capability": "catalogue",     "reason": "the LLM `pools:` section is core-owned config today, so the plane supplies no default section object" },
    { "field": "on_swap",           "planes_none": ["llm", "a2a"], "capability": "trust-pinning", "reason": "endpoint hot-swap on generation change is an MCP-endpoint concern; the LLM and A2A planes swap no per-endpoint object" },
    { "field": "parse_endpoint",    "planes_none": ["llm", "a2a"], "capability": "egress-auth",   "reason": "the parse-endpoint hook lowers the MCP client-endpoint config grammar; the LLM and A2A planes have no such endpoint section" },
    { "field": "lower_endpoint",    "planes_none": ["llm", "a2a"], "capability": "egress-auth",   "reason": "the lower-endpoint hook is the MCP client-endpoint lowering; the LLM and A2A planes lower no endpoint config" },
    { "field": "build_runtime",     "planes_none": ["a2a"],        "capability": "catalogue",     "reason": "the A2A plane is delegation-only today and builds no per-generation runtime object; LLM and MCP each build one" },
    { "field": "card_signing_domain","planes_none": ["llm", "mcp"],"capability": "trust-pinning", "reason": "agent-card signing identity is an A2A-only capability; the LLM and MCP planes issue no signed card" },
    { "field": "card_kid_prefix",   "planes_none": ["llm", "mcp"], "capability": "trust-pinning", "reason": "the card key-id prefix is part of A2A-only agent-card signing; the LLM and MCP planes mint no card key" }
  ]
}
